    feat(envoy-forge): single-hostname Gateway for the vdhwslin01 runner (chg-2026-10-05-031)
    
    ADR 0009, Argus C7/R9. Lands via hack/ops/chg-2026-10-05-031-envoy-forge-window.sh
    (2026-10-14 01:30, after the 01:05 gateway runner).
    
    - network/envoy-forge: own Envoy deployment (no mergeGateways), ONE HTTPS
      listener for forge.${SECRET_DOMAIN}, no :80, HTTPRoutes from devtools
      only, LB IP 172.16.2.251 via lbipam annotation (no spec.addresses; the
      status-keeper does not need to know this Gateway). 172.16.2.249 was
      dropped: it is a UniFi fixed-IP reservation.
    - No alias Service: exactly one Service may carry the owning-gateway labels
      (inc-2026-10-12-013).
    - external-dns-unifi target pinned to the envoy-internal IP, so the
      second parentRef adds no second forge A record on the UDM.
    - forgejo HTTPRoute: second parentRef envoy-forge/https.
    
    Checks: kustomize build + substitution, kubeconform 2/2, server-side
    dry-run OK. AGR-109: tests are the gate.
    
